            <rel name="summary" type="rst"/>
            <rel name="volitional-cause" type="rst"/>
            <rel name="conjunction" type="multinuc"/>
            <rel name="sequence" type="multinuc"/>
        </relations>
    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="34" relname="span">Well, outside of being ugly as sin, there are a few problems with the site, in terms of being senior-citizen user centered.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="38" relname="span">The first thing I noticed was that you have to use the scroll bar on the right to view the information below,</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="2" relname="circumstance">where you have the FAQ, contact information and more.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="37" relname="span">Most Web sites provide enough information on each page,</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="4" relname="elaboration">and then provide a link to a second page in order to continue reading.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="35" relname="span">Some non-technical seniors may have a problem with this feature.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="34" relname="evidence">The yellow, brown, blue, and white colors are all very boring and are a little hard on the eyes to read.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="39" relname="span">The design is suppose to look like a file folder of some type, which is almost a thing of the past now.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="33" relname="span">It may have been designed for those seniors who remember and still appreciate the good-old days</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="9" relname="circumstance">when paper files were put away in filing cabinets.</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="29" relname="conjunction">In a word, I think very little creativity was put into this site,</segment>
        <segment id="12" parent="29" relname="conjunction">and very few of the modern-day tools were used to build it.</segment>
        <segment id="13" parent="30" relname="sequence">Nothing stands out and catches my eye,</segment>
        <segment id="14" parent="30" relname="sequence">nothing guides my attention to a certain area of the site,</segment>
        <segment id="15" parent="30" relname="sequence">and nothing keeps me from falling asleep when looking at it for more than 5 minutes.</segment>
        <segment id="16" parent="27" relname="span">True, it does address the issues that seniors are concerned.</segment>
        <segment id="17" parent="16" relname="elaboration">Some seniors want to just find the facts, and dont really want all of the extras.</segment>
        <segment id="18" parent="26" relname="span">But, were not talking about window candy here,</segment>
        <segment id="19" parent="18" relname="circumstance">where special offers are flashing away in your face;</segment>
        <segment id="20" parent="25" relname="span">were talking about basic aesthetics,</segment>
        <segment id="21" parent="20" relname="elaboration">and there seems to be very little of that on this Web site</segment>
        <group id="22" type="span"/>
